# Build output
**/target/
**/.kotlin/
**/node_modules/

# Local tooling
.git/
.idea/
*.iml
*.ipr
*.iws

# Unneeded build context
docs/
ci/
# ...except the one file the Maven reactor needs: the parent pom lists
# ci/coverage-report as a module, so its pom must be in the context or the
# dependency-warmup layer cannot resolve the build at all. An exception inside an
# excluded directory is exactly what "!" is for.
!ci/coverage-report/pom.xml
# ci/sbom-postprocess is more than reactor-resolvable-only (unlike coverage-report above): both
# kotlin-invoice's and kotlin-xpdf's Dockerfiles COPY its full pom.xml + src, because it's an
# exec-maven-plugin PLUGIN dependency they actually run during `package`, not merely a module the
# reactor has to see. Un-ignoring the directory itself (not just files inside it) is required —
# a negated path under an excluded ancestor directory needs the ancestor negated too.
!ci/sbom-postprocess/
!ci/sbom-postprocess/**

# Environment files
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Logs and reports
*.log
mvn-jacoco.log
